  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance to Displaced Populations in Lac Province, Chad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chad is a landlocked country in Central Africa, which, in addition to being affected by a number of interlocking crises, shares borders with several crisis-affected countries. Since 2014, the crisis unfolding in the Lac province has been characterized by numerous challenging factors, such as insecurity, unpredictable heavy rainfall and flooding, large-scale and continuous population movements (internally displaced persons (IDPs), returnees) as well as community clashes and socioeconomic tensions. As of November 2022, there are still more than 239,575 displaced persons in 240 localities in the Lac Province. Based on the urgent need for humanitarian support, as well as the need for improved and reliable data and tracking of displacement, IOM is the implementing a three-fold response: 1) Strengthening of displacement data management to support decision-making, planning and direct assistance, through the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM)&#x2019;s Mobility tracking and continuation of the implementation of rapid biometric registration; 2) Provision and distribution of shelters and Non-Food Items (NFI) for the most vulnerable displaced households; and 3) Improving access to clean water and sanitation for vulnerable populations.</narrative>
  </description>
